                  <additions>
                     <list>
                        <item xml:id="a1">
                           <locus from="83ra" to="83rb"/>
                           <desc type="OwnershipNote">The ownership note states that the book belongs to <persName ref="PRS15568Tasfaya"><roleName type="rank">ḥalaqā</roleName> Tasfāy</persName> of <placeName ref="LOC7206Koholo">Kʷakʷalo</placeName>. 
                              It also mentions the names of his family: his wife <persName ref="PRS15569HirutaSellase">Ḫiruta Sǝllāse</persName>, his father <persName ref="PRS15570MazgabaSellase">Mazgaba Sǝllāse</persName>, 
                              his children <persName ref="PRS15571KinaSellase">Kina Sǝllāse</persName>, <persName ref="PRS15572HabtaSellase">Ḥabta Sǝllāse</persName>, <persName ref="PRS15573HaylaSellase">Ḫāyla Sǝllāse</persName>, 
                              <persName ref="PRS15574AmataSellase">ʾAmata Sǝllāse</persName>, <persName ref="PRS15575WalattaSellase">Walatta Sǝllāse</persName>,  <persName ref="PRS15576TebabaSellase">Ṭǝbaba Sǝllāse</persName>,
                              <persName ref="PRS15577LehkwataSellase">Lǝḥkʷǝta Sǝllāse</persName>, <persName ref="PRS15578SemrataSellase">Sǝmrata Sǝllāse</persName>, his mother <persName ref="PRS15579WalattaEgzi">Walatta ʾƎgziʾ</persName>, 
                              his grandmother <persName ref="PRS15580WalattaMaryam">Walatta Māryām</persName>, the sister of his mother <persName ref="PRS15581AmataSeyon"> ʿĀmata Ṣǝyon</persName>, 
                              his sister <persName ref="PRS15582WalattaBerhan">Walatta Bǝrhān</persName>, and his brother <persName ref="PRS15583GabraGiyorgis"><roleName type="rank">ḫalaqā</roleName> ʾAbbāy</persName>. 
                              It is written in <ref target="#h1"/>. The note contains a tamallas-sign, in the shape of
                              two perpendicular lines, indicating where the omission, written above, belongs: <locus target="#83ra8"/>.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ዝመጽሐፍ፡ አእማደ፡ ምስጢር፡ ዘሐለቃ፡ ተስፋይ፡
                              ኰኰሎ፡ ዘውእቱ፡ ገብረ፡ ስላሴ፡ <add place="above">ወብእሲቱ፡ ኂሩተ፡ ስላሴ፡</add> ወአቡሁ፡ መዝገበ፡ ስላሴ፡ ወደቂቁ፡ ኪነ፡
                              ስላሴ፡ ሐብተ፡ ስላሴ፡ ኃይለ፡ ስላሴ፡ አመተ፡ ስላሴ፡ ወለተ፡ ስላሴ፡ ጥበበ፡ ስላሴ፡ ልሕኵተ፡ ስላሴ፡
                              ስምረተ፡ ስላሴ፡ ወእሙ፡ ወለተ፡ እግዚእ፡ ወእማ፡ ወለተ፡ ማርያም፡ ወእህታ፡ ዓመተ፡ ጽዮን፡ ወወለታ፡ ወለተ፡
                              ብርሃን፡ ወእሁኁ፡ ገብረ፡ ጊዎርጊስ፡ ዘውእቱ፡ ኃለቃ፡ አባይ፡ ዘሰረቆ፡ ወዘፈሀቆ፡ ወዘተአገሎ፡ በኃይል፡
                              ዘዕ<add place="above">ን</add>በለ፡ ፈቃደ፡ እግዚኡ፡ ውጉዘ፡ ለይኩን፡ በስልጣነ፡ ጴጥሮ<add place="above">ስ</add>፡ ወጳውሎስ፡ ከመ፡ አርዮስ፡
                              ወመቅደልዮስ።</q>
                           <q xml:lang="en">This book of ʾAʿmāda mǝśṭir is of ḥalaqā Tasfāya of Kʷakʷalo, who is Gabra Sǝllāse. His wife is
                              Ḫiruta Sǝllāse and his father Mazgaba Sǝllāse, and his children Kina
                              Sǝllāse, Ḥabta Sǝllāse, Ḫāyla Sǝllāse, ʾAmata Sǝllāse, Walatta
                              Sǝllāse, Ṭǝbaba Sǝllāse, Lǝḥkʷǝta Sǝllāse, Sǝmrata Sǝllāse, and his
                              mother Walatta ʾƎgziʾ, and her mother Walatta Māryām, and her sister
                              ʿĀmata Ṣǝyon, and her daughter Walatta Bǝrhān, and his brother Gabra
                              Giyorgis that is ḫalaqā ʾAbbāy. May the one who stole it or erased it
                              or took it by force without the permission of the owner be
                              excommunicated by the authority of Peter and Paul like Arius and
                              Macedonius. </q>
                        </item>
                        
